{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"karmic-balsamic-iguanodon","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Discovered while fixing the ubuntu/py3.11 hang (89d5-61da-b621-47f8): the shared Verified/branch-CI suite in _build-and-test.yml now carries --timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread, but the other CI pytest invocations still have NO per-test hang guard:\n\n- .github/workflows/external-integration.yml lines ~219, ~369, ~472, ~566 (external / llm_live tiers)\n- .github/workflows/structured-output-baseline.yml ~105\n- .github/workflows/test.yml ~125 (pytest -m external)\n\nThese are non-xdist live-service lanes, so a blanket 300s could flake a legitimately slow live-LLM/Jira call — pick a larger, tier-appropriate ceiling (and possibly --timeout-method=thread) rather than copying 300s. Lower priority than the Verified-gate fix; filed so the class is not silently left half-guarded. Consider widening test_shared_pytest_suite_has_a_per_test_hang_guard (or a sibling) to cover these files once a ceiling is chosen.","id":"d835-1846-95d1-4d84","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Extend the pytest per-test hang guard to the external/live-service CI lanes"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786131596759086001,"uuid":"402ce713-a1bb-4c7c-8e22-4ab1b89a2f63"}